    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0232" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/229: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winslow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-24T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 24—9:47
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>95. Buero as head of Uruguayan delegation to the Preparatory Disarmament
                    Commission having received directly from the Secretariat of the League a copy of
                    my letter of April 8th to Drummond<anchor n="93" xml:id="d74-f1"/> told me at a
                    private interview in his opinion the attitude of the Department was entirely
                    correct and that he could be counted on to <pb facs="0233" n="101"
                        xml:id="pg101"/> do all in his power to support our views with regard to the
                    organization of the work of the Conference when it meets.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Winslow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d74-f1" n="93" xml:id="d74-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 54, Apr. 7, 1926, to the Chargé in Switzerland, <ref
